      "side": 1,
      "message": "For context, without this define, Vulkan benchmarks fail at runtime with:\n\n```\nsrc/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkGpu.cpp:199: fatal error: \"No supplied vulkan memory allocator and unable to create one internally.\"\n```\n\nSee https://skia.googlesource.com/skia/+/c3fbd20fbc7d3662dd31a0e4139226d2951d1ae4/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkGpu.cpp#199.\n\nThis behavior can be traced to the `VulkanAMDMemoryAllocator::Make()` implementation here: https://skia.googlesource.com/skia/+/c3fbd20fbc7d3662dd31a0e4139226d2951d1ae4/src/gpu/vk/VulkanAMDMemoryAllocator.cpp#17, which always returns `nullptr`.\n\nNote that the above implementation is within a `#ifndef SK_USE_VMA` block. By setting `SK_USE_VMA`, I\u0027m opting into the `#else` branch of that block, which provides a \"real\" `VulkanAMDMemoryAllocator::Make()` implementation.\n\nI\u0027ll ask Greg / Nicolette for their opinion.",
      "parentUuid": "0fe05759_c7cc2614",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "2684d3bc41e28ccd659853f0ab51b57336105fb2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
